# Angular component file layout

Always create components as a folder with these four files (never inline `template` / `styles`):

```text
feature-name/
  ├── feature-name.component.ts
  ├── feature-name.component.html
  ├── feature-name.component.scss
  └── feature-name.component.spec.ts
```

## Rules

- Use `templateUrl` and `styleUrl` (or `styleUrls`), not inline `template` / `styles`.
- Prefer `standalone: true` unless an existing pattern differs.
- Generate with CLI when possible: `ng g c path/to/name --standalone`
- Do not put multiple unrelated components in one file.

## `.component.ts` file order

```text
imports
@Component({ … })
export class … { … }
```

**Nothing between imports and `@Component`** except when unavoidable — then only `type` / `class` / `function` declarations (no `const` catalogs, no mapped data, no logic).

Prefer row/view types in `models/*.ts` (e.g. `LocationTableRow` in `models/location.ts`) so the component file goes straight from imports to `@Component`.
